<Base lang="en" alternatePath="/waribashi/support/" title="Support — Waribashi - Chopsticks Battle" description="Support for Waribashi - Chopsticks Battle">
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>Waribashi - Chopsticks Battle</p>

    <div>
      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, bug reports, or suggestions about Waribashi - Chopsticks Battle, please contact us at the email address below.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Meowtaverse Games (operated by Tokusei Noborio)</strong>
          <br />
          Email:
          <a href="mailto:tokusei@meowtaverse-games.com">
            tokusei@meowtaverse-games.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Frequently asked questions (FAQ)</h2>

        <h3>Q. How do I learn the rules?</h3>
        <p>
          Tap “How to Play” at the bottom of the app’s home screen to view the tutorial. It explains the basic rules and controls.
        </p>

        <h3>Q. Why can’t I play online?</h3>
        <p>
          Online battles require an internet connection. Please check that Wi-Fi or mobile data is enabled. Matchmaking also requires another player.
        </p>

        <h3>Q. Can I remove ads?</h3>
        <p>There is currently no option to remove ads in the app version. The browser version does not display ads.</p>

        <h3>Q. How can I delete my data?</h3>
        <p>
          Game settings data is stored only on your device and is deleted when you uninstall the app.
          In the browser version, clearing the site data for meowtaverse-games.com (including waribashi.meowtaverse-games.com) in your browser deletes the settings and identifiers stored in your browser.
          Online battle room records typically expire 24 hours after the last activity and are then deleted automatically
          (except records used only by the Android and iOS versions 1.1.0 and earlier, which includes the iOS versions available on the App Store as of October 18, 2026).
          The anonymous authentication account (user ID) itself is not deleted automatically.
          To request deletion, please email tokusei@meowtaverse-games.com. We delete online battle room records and anonymous authentication user IDs upon request.
          For details, see <a href="/en/waribashi/privacy/#:~:text=6.%20Data%20storage%20and%20deletion">Section 6, “Data storage and deletion”</a> of the privacy policy and,
          for requests from parents and guardians, <a href="/en/waribashi/privacy/#:~:text=7.%20Children%E2%80%99s%20privacy">Section 7, “Children’s privacy”</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>System requirements</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>iOS 13.0 or later</li>
          <li>Android 7.0 or later</li>
          <li>Browser version (https://waribashi.meowtaverse-games.com/): the latest Chrome, Safari, Edge, or Firefox</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
